Generally, if any condition <math>\phi</math> in the wave is carried forward unchanged with velocity <math>\text{U}</math>, the change of <math>\phi</math> at a given point in time <math>dt</math> is equal to the change of <math>\phi</math> as we go ''back'' along the curve a distance <math>dx = \text{U}dt</math> at the beginning of <math>dt</math>.
